    "m2_prompt_trader_proposal_original": "**Action**: Hold\n\n**Reasoning**: The evidence is genuinely balanced, supporting a Hold. The long-term structural case is intact \u2014 JPM trades 16.5% above its 200-day SMA, the 50-day SMA is rising ($141.94\u2192$151.85), and the fortress balance sheet ($3.9T assets, $317B equity) supports maintaining exposure. However, the near-term tactical setup is weak: MACD histogram has been negative for 11 consecutive sessions, the stock made a lower high ($161.60 vs. $163.46) on elevated volume (distribution pattern), and RSI at 64.32 is elevated while price stalls. The risk-reward at $161.60 is asymmetric \u2014 only +1.7% upside to $164.32 resistance vs. -6% downside to the 50-day SMA at $151.85. Macro data (news, sentiment, Fed policy) is unavailable, so aggressive positioning is not justified. This is not a Sell given the intact trend and balance sheet quality, but not a Buy given the poor near-term risk-reward and persistent negative momentum divergence.\n\n**Entry Price**: 161.6\n\n**Stop Loss**: 151.85\n\n**Position Sizing**: Maintain current position; moderate sizing given unavailable macro data. Do not add aggressively at $161.60.\n\nFINAL TRANSACTION PROPOSAL: **HOLD**",
